<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khust</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khust is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carpathian-ruthenia">Zakarpattia</a> Oblast in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, on the Tysa river below the ruins of a medieval castle. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-vienna-award">First Vienna Award</a> gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzhhorod">Uzhhorod</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> in 1938, it became the capital of autonomous Carpatho-Ukraine. There, on 15 March 1939, the Carpatho-Ukrainian diet declared independence, a day before Hungarian troops took the town.</p></div>
